{"verdict":"approve","summary":"Re-examining the actual call site (set_height shrink branch) confirms the fix is correct: the old viewport rows are cleared by the caller, and repaint_history_tail now clears exactly top..visible_rows == the draw span, so no terminal-scrolled content in 0..top is blanked. The u16 cast is safe (row <= viewport.y which is u16), tests verify the clear==draw invariant, and the no-clamp path still full-clears. My prior needs-changes is dropped.","concede":["I had suspected the reduced clear span could leave stale content in the small-history/no-scrollback case, but re-reading set_height shows the shrink branch pre-clears the old viewport rows (old_y..old_y+old_height) before calling repaint_history_tail, so the only uncleared rows 0..top are genuinely terminal-scrolled content that must be preserved — exactly the regression being fixed.","I had no concrete finding against the row-as-u16 cast; visible_rows is viewport.y (u16) so the range is in-bounds."],"maintain":[],"findings":[]}
